<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>On a town map (1 unit = 1 km) the bus park is at <m>A({1},\,{5})</m> and the hospital at <m>B({-5},\,{-5})</m>.</p><p>(a) Write <m>\overrightarrow{AB}</m> as a column vector.</p><div><m>\overrightarrow{AB} =</m> <fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/>  </div><p>(b) The market M is at the end of the vector <m>{\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m> drawn from the school <m>C({-4},\,{2})</m>, so <m>\overrightarrow{CM} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -2 \end{array}\right)}</m>. Find the coordinates of M.</p><div>M = ( <fillin characters="4" name="ans2"/> , <fillin characters="4" name="ans3"/> )  </div><div/></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) <m>\overrightarrow{AB}</m> is end minus start: B's coordinates minus A's. Across: <m>{-5} - {1} = {-6}</m>; up: <m>{-5} - {5} = {-10}</m>. So <m>\overrightarrow{AB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -10 \end{array}\right)}</m>.</p><p>(b) Start at C and make the moves of the vector: M = <m>({-4} + ({-2}),\ {2} + ({-2}))</m> <m>= ({-6},\,{0})</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\left(\begin{array}{c} -6 \\ -10 \end{array}\right)</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-6</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>0</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>